WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:05.940
<b>July 15th       00:04 AM</b>

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.510
Are you the so-called Niwaka Samurai?

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.370
Yeah, that'd be me.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.450
You're shorter than I expected.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.700
You look like a girl.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.230
I was told I'd be assigned 
a target at this meeting.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.540
Who am I supposed to kill?

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.710
Me.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.570
Huh?

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.140
Damn it!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.680
If you beat me, I'll pay you 
what we agreed upon.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.600
This guy's good!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.860
<b>A Few Hours Earlier</b>

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.860
Hey, old man.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.910
Banba's passed out.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.320
He said he has an early start tomorrow.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.870
Right. The Oiyama event is tomorrow.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.470
You calling about a job?

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.870
I can handle it, if you want.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.420
<i>Nah, not even you can handle this one.</i>

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.500
Why not?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.010
<i>The client specifically asked 
for the Niwaka Samurai.</i>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.420
<i>He says he'll pay twice the normal fee.</i>

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.550
Oh?

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.580
Well, we'll just have to turn them down.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.000
<i>Oh, Banba just got up.</i>

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.270
<i>He went to the bathroom.</i>

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.230
Oh, yeah?

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.420
<i>Hey, Banba!</i>

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.490
<i>Do you feel up to a job?</i>

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.510
<i>Okay.</i>

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:32.940
<i>He says he'll do it.</i>

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.510
He wants me to get the time and place.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.560
<i>Shit! What the hell?</i>

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.750
<i>I shouldn't have taken interest!</i>

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.730
What, is that all you've got?

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:55.180
You'd better not be an easy kill!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.250
<b>#06   Pinch Hitter</b>

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.340
Lin-chan's gone.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.870
Well, he's a grown man, after all.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.470
I bet he's out having fun somewhere.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.990
What's wrong, hitmen hitman?!

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.460
You're not as tough as they say!

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.560
Ow!

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.590
Whoa, there.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.100
Damn it, this thing's too hard to handle!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.180
Huh.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.360
Wha—

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.400
Hey! You bastard!

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.710
Huh?!

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.160
Hey! What the hell?!

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.610
What the...

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.780
Shit, shit, shit!

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.220
All good.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.980
Sweet dreams.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.220
We caught the Niwaka Samurai!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.590
Yeah, it was worth siccing that 
ninja bastard on him, after all.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.190
The hundred million will be ours!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.490
<i>Shit, I've gone and done it again...</i>

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:07.100
<i>Banba's gonna lecture me again.</i>

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:11.450
<b>01:07 AM</b>

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.660
Hey, look! Here it comes!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.260
Here what comes?

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.820
A torture job!

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.160
Remember how I posted on 
Shadyjob.com the other day?

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.630
Oh, that.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.960
Good for you.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.540
Let's see...

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:28.890
"We need you to torture a man 
to get information out of him.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.510
He won't even scream for us,
no matter how much we beat him up.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.820
Get back to us ASAP, thanks."

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.560
Thank God for online business deals.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.730
"Send me the info and photo 
of the target for a quote."

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.230
Sent.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.490
<b>3:53 AM</b>

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.970
This is definitely the car.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.650
Good job finding it.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:56.870
I asked an anonymous hacker to track it down 
using security cameras around the city.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.570
I got ripped off because it was urgent, but hey.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.380
Thanks for your business!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.660
Huh? Hey...

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.010
Hang on a sec, Sarucchi!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.660
How dare you steal my prey 
out from under my nose?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.790
S-Sorry! We shouldn't have!

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:22.110
We lost our jobs and we're flat broke.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.270
Like I care.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:28.190
Where's the Niwaka Samurai?

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.170
You bastards!

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.380
What have you done?!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.490
I was supposed to be the one to kill him!

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.300
U-Um, he's a fake.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.630
A fake?

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:55.980
What do you mean?

00:06:55.980 --> 00:07:01.850
I once talked to someone who was 
blinded in one eye by the Niwaka Samurai.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.500
This one looks really different 
from how the guy described him.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.270
This guy even admitted 
he wasn't the real deal,

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:13.240
so we tried torturing 
him to make him talk.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.740
And then he just... died.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.580
But it wasn't our fault!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.840
He wouldn't talk no matter 
how much we beat him up,

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.910
so we called in a pro.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.650
But he was, like, the worst torturer ever!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.630
A fake?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.620
Huh?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.880
What the hell?!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.300
The bastard's screwing with me, damn it!

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.180
A fake?! Seriously?!

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.460
Calm down, Sarucchi.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.910
If this guy knew the real deal,

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.190
maybe we can use this.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.830
There you are, Banba!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.990
Huh?

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.370
Hey, boss. What's wrong?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.170
Just come with me.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.450
I thought something was off...

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.090
After all, why would you take 
a job right before the Oiyama?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.510
Who would've guessed that 
Lin would go in your stead?

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.450
Huh?

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.810
"If you want to save him,

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.470
come to this location by 4:30 AM."

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:27.710
Though it may already be 
too late, from the look of it.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:31.140
I'm gonna go, boss.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.390
It doesn't matter if he's dead or alive.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.330
Lin being left all on his own is too sad.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.490
I've gotta go get him.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:46.890
Banba, the event's about to start.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.880
Sorry, I'm needed elsewhere.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.020
Huh? You've gotta be kidding.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.840
Banba! Banba!

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:05.190
<b>4:41 AM</b>

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.360
The one earlier looked like a woman,

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.030
and this one looks pretty weird, too.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.990
Are you the real Niwaka Samurai?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:22.970
Yes, I am.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.080
Where's the man from the photo?

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.740
Yes, Lee-san.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:34.350
As I reported, the Niwaka 
Samurai will soon...

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.050
What? Well...

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.600
Sorry, he's already dead.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:46.310
I wasn't the one who did the deed, though.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.970
A pretty face.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:51.650
Almost as if the mortician's already 
worked on him for his funeral.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:55.890
Hey.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.620
Draw your sword.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.940
The Yamakasa's about to start.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:05.250
I don't have time to play with you.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.660
Give up on the festival.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:11.130
If you insist on going to it, 
kill me before you leave.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:18.090
Well done.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.760
Your job ends here.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.720
We'll be taking the Niwaka Samurai.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.940
You're with the Kakyu Association...

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.690
What kind of joke is—

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.830
Restrain him.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.980
What's going on?!

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.070
You guys are the ones who 
asked me to kill him!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.980
The circumstances have changed.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:46.050
The chairman wants to do the deed himself.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.190
So yeah, that's what happened.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.710
Sorry, Sarucchi!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.390
To hell with that!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:53.210
He's mine!

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.360
Now, now, Sarucchi...

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:00.090
Don't worry. We'll pay the 
price we agreed upon.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.950
Hey! Wait!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.810
I said wait!

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.610
Just bear with it, Sarucchi.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.640
How dare you?!

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.420
I didn't ask for this!

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.900
I'll kill you!

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:17.360
Okay, if that'll make you feel better.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:26.820
Yes, we have captured the Niwaka Samurai.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:27.910
I see.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.740
Prepare the execution.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.190
I'll head over now.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.490
Oh, you're leaving?

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.380
After making me wait so long?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.750
What a cruel man.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:44.790
Don't worry. I'll only leave 
once I've satisfied you.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:47.690
That's a promise.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.060
Shit, shit, shit!

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:52.680
Sarucchi.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:59.070
Look. I put a transmitter on 
the Kakyu Association's car.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.180
There's something more important to you

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:05.910
than a hundred million yen, isn't there?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.340
You should've told me sooner!

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.830
You're not my partner for nothing!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.830
Hey, how are you feeling?

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.630
Like a corpse.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.090
God, it reeks of corpse inside this thing.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.120
Nothing I could do about that.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.680
I carried your body double in that thing.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.560
Anyway, what a surprise that was.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:32.180
One minute, I have this duo threatening 
me with maximum torture,

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.370
and the next, you show up.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.540
That's my line.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.830
There I was, happy to finally 
be getting a torture job,

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.950
and then you show up on the target photo.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.490
We had to scramble to formulate a plan

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.500
to take a body double over there

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.450
and return with Lin.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:55.580
It was a challenge to find a body 
that looked like you so quickly.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.370
It sure was.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.420
We had to make the body 
look like you in a hurry.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.010
Okay, okay. I'm grateful.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.870
Can I say just one more thing?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.620
Passing yourself off as the Niwaka 
Samurai is too far of a stretch.

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:13.100
Fine, my bad.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:16.440
You can just be yourself, Lin.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.180
Jiro-chan told me the same 
thing a long time ago.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:29.780
Oh, shut it.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:33.770
I don't need a lecture from you, too, brat.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:38.910
Well, guess I'll go use the restroom.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:46.010
Jeez...

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.950
He just can't ever be honest, huh?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.680
Banba Zenji

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.730
I bet the festival's started already.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.900
Oh, hey. That you, old man?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.120
<i>Lin! You're alive!</i>

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.400
Huh?

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.490
Damn that moron Ban!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.080
<b>Kakyu 
Association     Hakata Branch</b>

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.370
Hey, what time is it?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:17.430
Shut up.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:23.050
Damn, my team's float is probably 
in the race right about now.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.460
Who the hell are you?!

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:43.520
Sorry.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.540
But why are you helping me?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.240
If you die, I can't kill you.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.590
What're you aiming at, 
you lame-ass, zero-aim ninja?

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:08.990
Shut up!

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.250
I just need to warm up!

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.490
Shit.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.950
Flee to fight another day.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.110
Bastards!

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:34.160
Capture them!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.130
Kill them if necessary!

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.010
Lee-san, we have a problem.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.460
What? Chairman Wang?

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:51.700
Forget those two.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.610
Let's go!

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.810
They gave up?

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.470
Oh, well.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.250
We can finally continue 
what we started earlier.

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:04.480
I'll have to take a rain check.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:07.070
Can you call it off for today?

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.530
What? Are you scared you'll lose to me?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.870
"Scared"?

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.860
Interesting word choice.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:32.620
I admit I got my hopes up
when I was invited to a hotel,

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.490
but it seems I'm only here to help.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.080
Sorry.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.810
But thanks to you, my job went well.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.820
How'd you get the weapon in?

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.020
Rumor has it that every 
woman who lies in his bed

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.430
is subjected to a body cavity search.

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.630
You're not wrong.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:56.450
But no one noticed the poison I put on these.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:59.200
You're a scary woman, Sayuri-san.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:05.920
So who made the insane request to 
assassinate the Kakyu Association's boss?

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.010
An insane man.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.520
You're not bad-looking.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.230
Neither are you.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.490
Perfect trajectory!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.960
He hit it right back to me?!

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:58.340
That was a close call.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.060
Here, grab this.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.970
Why are you doing this?

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.050
I owe you.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:10.370
That wasn't why I helped you.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.450
Besides, if I let you fall here,

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.400
you'll disrupt the Yamakasa.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:19.610
So let's call today a draw, shall we?

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:33.550
Is this about right to avenge 
the fake Niwaka Samurai?

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.800
I guess.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.060
Avengers only mete out what 
was dealt to their clients.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:39.570
But...

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.720
It's always possible to 
overdo it by mistake.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.420
After all, some hitmen kill

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.470
the wrong person altogether 
because they have a similar name.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.130
<i>Oh, hey. Is that you, Sarucchi?</i>

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.700
<i>I'm glad you're alive!</i>

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.340
What the hell?

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.860
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:04.820
<i>So did you beat the Niwaka Samurai?</i>

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:07.190
No, it was a draw.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.290
<i>Huh? How?</i>

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.370
Hey, Nao.

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.590
This city's pretty damn interesting.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:25.290
Celebrate, Wakamatsu-sama...

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.350
Banba!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:30.270
Lin-chan, what's wrong?

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.450
That's my line!

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.620
You didn't pick up, no matter 
how many times I called!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.570
Oops, I put it on silent and forgot about it.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:41.700
Huh?

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.660
When did I get this?

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.780
You only just noticed it?

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:53.370
I heard you ran out after me,
thinking I'd been killed.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.890
That's an exaggeration.

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:59.310
You thought I'd get done in that easily?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.650
You're underestimating me.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.720
I wasn't underestimating you.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.180
I was just worried.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.950
Sorry for surprising you.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.380
And for pretending to 
be the Niwaka Samurai.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.940
Well, all's well that ends well.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.860
But...

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:24.340
The Yamakasa's over!

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:29.110
And it had to be the day of the Oiyama event...

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:32.000
I'd been looking forward to it all year.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.800
So what?

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.460
There's always next year.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.890
That's not the point.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:40.420
This year's Oiyama <i>only</i> happens this year.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:45.050
Today was supposed to be my reward 
for all my hard work over the last year.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.010
Forget it.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:48.510
Let's go.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:51.500
We can eat ramen on the way home.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.230
I can pay today.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.170
With spicy pollock roe on rice.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.520
Not that again.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.400
<b>Ogura Fried 
Udons</b>

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.400
<b>Hakata Tonkotsu 
Ramens</b>

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:08.270
Good work today.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.380
That pitcher's got such poor aim 
that it's hard to hit the ball.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.460
Yeah, well...

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.670
Hey, their manager's a hottie!

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.380
Whoa! You're right!

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.520
Huh?

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:23.560
Isn't that Banba-san's former...

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:24.380
Huh?

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.720
That was close.

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:33.390
What's with the attitude?!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.730
You almost hit me in the head!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:36.900
Shut up!

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.560
Just get in your position already!

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:40.770
You little...

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.480
Uh-oh. He snapped.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:44.530
Don't!

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:45.310
Banba-san!

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:47.160
You almost hit me!

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.240
At least take your hat off!

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.330
He's as insane as always.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.510
You lame-ass, zero-aim pitcher!

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.530
Shut up!

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:57.710
I just need to warm up!

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:06.750
I have something I'd like you to look into.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.220
Counter Cyber Crime Unit?

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:08.620
Ew, that's too raw.

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:09.450
Hey, what the hell?!

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:11.660
I'll contact you if I need help.

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.250
They sure did a number on you.

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:14.990
I was killed.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
#07  Lead-off Hitter
